User: There are two possible triangles with $AB = 13,$ $BC = 10,$ and $A = 40^\circ.$  One of them is shown below.  What is the sum of the two possible values of $\angle B,$ in degrees?

[asy]
unitsize (1 cm);

pair A, B, C;

A = (0,0);
B = 5*dir(40);
C = (5,0);

